{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.SubstrateParameterUnique","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.SubstrateParameterUnique","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.SubstrateParameter"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SubstrateParameter.unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SubstrateParameter.unique","kind":"theorem","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter-unique.lean#L33-L62","doc":"Uniqueness of the substrate parameter (conditional on shared QOU\n    origin).\n\nGiven two substrate parameters for the same base $M$ that arise from\nthe same underlying QOU (encoded by `SameQouOrigin`), their\nunderlying field values coincide pointwise. The proof follows from:\n(1) intrinsic spectral decomposition of the braiding $c_{V,V}$\n    (the splitting $V \\otimes V = S^2 V \\oplus \\Lambda^2 V$ is\n    canonical, so the eigenvalue pair $\\{\\lambda_+, \\lambda_-\\}$\n    is intrinsic);\n(2) the Hecke relation pinning the unordered pair as\n    $\\{q, -q^{-1}\\}$;\n(3) positivity of the induced dagger selecting the positive\n    representative.\n\nThe `SameQouOrigin` hypothesis stands in for the as-yet-unformalized\nQOU structure: once Ch 2's axioms are in scope as a Lean type, the\nhypothesis becomes derivable from any pair of QOU instances on $M$\nand the theorem upgrades to unconditional uniqueness.\n\nRef: [kassel1995] https://doi.org/10.1007/978-1-4612-0783-2\n     §XIV — braid group representations from R-matrices, combined\n     with the positivity constraint from the QOU dagger structure.\n","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:thm:substrate-parameter-unique","label":"thm:substrate-parameter-unique","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter-unique.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SubstrateParameter.SameQouOrigin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SubstrateParameter.SameQouOrigin","kind":"def","line":20,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter-unique.lean#L20-L31","doc":"Witness that two `SubstrateParameter` instances arise from the\nsame underlying QOU.  The narrative content of this predicate is\n\"shared braiding $c_{V,V}$ + shared Hecke relation + shared\npositive-definite dagger\" — exactly the data that, per Ch 2,\npins the substrate-parameter field uniquely.  Until the full\nQuantumObservableUniverse structure is axiomatised in Lean we\ntake its operative consequence — field equality — as the\n*definition* of `SameQouOrigin`.  Once Ch 2's axioms land, this\ndef will be promoted to a theorem deriving field equality from\na richer same-QOU witness. ","signatureChunk":0}]}